% CASE · Four Rooms — a score fitted to an existing 29.6 s film (huashu-motion's own promo, 128 bpm, D major)
% Spotting: the film has seven scenes; the score hits only the four that matter and lets the other cuts
% flow over the music — rooms (5.45 s, label), studio (13.0 s, label), made (20.35 s, the impact
% triplet) and logo (27.0 s, the chime), the last two given by OM.music({ marks: { made: 20.35, logo: 27 } }).
% om sound reported the tempo bends: rooms→studio −0.5 %, studio→made −4.1 %, made→logo +0.7 %. The first
% draft bent +7.7 % into the logo; one bar was cut to 3/4 instead of pushing the tempo.
% bars 1–3  an 11-beat intro (a 3/4 bar first so it starts at 0.25 s): piano eighths, strings swell,
%           snare build + riser into the rooms; the last beat empty.
% bars 4–7  one bar per room: synth-pluck sixteenths as the hook, pop kit, synth bass eighths.
% bars 8–11 studio: back to the opening piano figure and hats only; from bar 10 the layers grow back
%           as the film's sound scene grows; a 3/4 bar pushes early into the chorus.
% bars 12–14 made: strings sing the hook in octaves (the motif 5–1–2–3 extended), piano 3+3+2, horns.
% bars 15–16 end → logo: a pluck arpeggio under the logo assembling, piano pickup A–D–E landing on F#
%           with the chime, everything held.
